<p>In the photo above, you can just make out the dam that creates this lake. 
It's a simple earthen dam; there's no sign of electric power generation or even 
control; so the purpose of the dam must have been simply to create this lake.</p>

<p>At one point along the shore trail we came upon some logs floating in the 
water. Zach played on them for at least half-an-hour.</p>

<img src="SANY0393.JPG">

<img src="SANY0395.JPG" alt="Bear Canyon Lake.">

<p>Back at camp, the kids played a little flag football.</p>

<img src="SANY0402.JPG" alt="Zach, future gridiron hero.">

<p>I let Zach take the camera for a bit and take shots of anything that 
interested him. Thank God for digital cameras and 1gb memory chips!</p>

